 "money": -2.59}, "rating_margin": -15.22, "sigma_race": 7.0, "sigma_total": 7.73, "baseline_margin": -11.69, "analyst_adjustment": -2.31, "key_factors": ["R+10 district with incumbent Lance Gooden seeking reelection", "Lopsided money: $1.33M on hand for Gooden vs about $5K for Chelsey Hockett", "All nine expert ratings at Safe/Solid or Likely R; markets price a Democratic win near 5%", "House Ethics Committee investigation into Gooden is the main risk"], "rationale": "Gooden pairs a strongly Republican district with a million-dollar war chest against a challenger who has raised under $13,000, while every major rater places the seat in the Safe or Solid Republican column and markets price a Democratic win around 5%. The House Ethics investigation is the only notable wrinkle and is unlikely to overcome these fundamentals.", "watch": "A damaging finding from the House Ethics probe, combined with an unusually strong Democratic midterm wave, is the main scenario that could narrow the race.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Lance Gooden (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas's 5th District leans firmly Republican, and incumbent Lance Gooden is seeking another term after winning renomination. Every major race rater places the seat in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrat Chelsey Hockett roughly a one-in-twenty chance. The financial picture is lopsided: Gooden has raised about $1.3 million and holds $1.3 million on hand, while Hockett has raised under $13,000. No public polls of the general election are available, so the outlook rests on the district's partisan lean, the incumbent's advantages, and the consensus of professional ratings.\n\nThe main wrinkle is a House Ethics Committee investigation into Gooden reported in July, which has not visibly altered the race's shape. Absent an unusually strong Democratic wave or a damaging ethics finding, the district's fundamentals point to a comfortable Republican win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0352, "margin": -14.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0406, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -14.0}]}